-- title:
--   Logarithmic weight bound for twisted orbital double-coset integrals
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subseteq L$ be number fields with $L/K$ Galois, let $\nu_{Z,L}$ be a Haar measure on the idele unit group $(\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$, let $D$ be a descent datum consisting of a homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ to the ring automorphisms of $\mathbb{A}_L$ compatible with the action on $L$ and acting continuously, let $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ be such that every element of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$, let $S$ be a finite set of finite places of $K$, and let $\varphi_a$ and $(\varphi_{S,v})_v$ be complex-valued functions on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the infinite adeles of $L$, respectively of $L \otimes_K K_v$. Let $H$ be a closed subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ whose elements are exactly the $h$ with $h_{10} = h_{01} = 0$ and with $\sigma(h)h^{-1}$ central, $\sigma$ acting entrywise through $D$, and let $\mu_H$ be a right-invariant Haar measure on $H$. Then for every finite set $T$ of finite places of $K$ and every choice $w_v$ of a place of $L$ above each $v$, there are $C \ge 0$ and $A \in \mathbb{N}$ such that the following holds for every family $\rho_v \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L_{w_v})$, every $\varphi$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ and every $\varphi_f$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the finite adeles which form a semi-local factorisation relative to $S \cup T$ (i.e. $\varphi_a$ is a compactly supported smooth archimedean factor, $\varphi_f$ is locally constant with compact support, $\varphi(g) = \varphi_a(g_\infty)\varphi_f(g_f)$, $\varphi_f$ vanishes unless all semi-local components outside $S \cup T$ are integral and otherwise equals the product over $S \cup T$ of the prescribed factors) where the factor at $v \in T$ is the indicator of the double coset $\mathcal{K}_v \rho_v \mathcal{K}_v$, $\mathcal{K}_v$ the set of elements of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ integral together with their inverses and $\rho_v$ taken through the embedding of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L_{w_v})$ into $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the finite adeles followed by the semi-local component map, and the factor at $v \notin T$ is $\varphi_{S,v}$: for every $t \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ with $t_{10} = t_{01} = 0$ and $N_{L/K}(t_{00}/t_{11}) \neq 1$, the lower integral over the orbit quotient of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ by $H$, with respect to the quotient measure built from adelic Haar measure and $\mu_H$, of the weight $\bigl|-\log \mathrm{ht}(y) - \log \mathrm{ht}(wy)\bigr|$ (with $y$ a representative of the class, $\mathrm{ht}$ the adelic height, product of the archimedean and finite local heights, and $w$ the image in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ of the antidiagonal involution) times the inner $\nu_{Z,L}$-integral of $\|\varphi(y^{-1} t \,\sigma(zy))\|$ over central scalars $z$, is at most $C \prod_{v \in T}\bigl(1 + \log \mu'_v(\mathcal{K}_v \rho_v \mathcal{K}_v)\bigr)^A$ times the same double integral without the weight, $\mu'_v$ being the Haar measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ normalised to give $\mathcal{K}_v$ measure one.
--
--   This is the step that removes the height weight from a twisted orbital integral on the $\sigma$-diagonal quotient, at the cost of a power of a logarithm of the Hecke double-coset volumes: the weighted class integral is dominated by the unweighted one. It feeds into the assembly bounding the sum of unweighted and weighted double-coset orbital terms by a power of the measures.
